Procedure
Step 1: Open CloudShell
Login to AWS Console.
Click CloudShell terminal icon on top-right.
Step 2: Open EC2 Instance Details
Go to EC2 Dashboard.
Select running Linux instance.
Click Connect.
Open SSH Client tab.
Step 3: Copy SSH Command

Example:

ssh -i "key.pem" ubuntu@public-ip
Step 4: Upload Key File to CloudShell
In CloudShell click Actions (+).
Select Upload File.
Upload .pem file.
Step 5: Give Permission to Key

Run:

chmod 400 key.pem
Step 6: Connect to EC2

Run copied SSH command:

ssh -i "key.pem" ubuntu@public-ip
Step 7: Verify Connection

Run:

whoami
Observation
CloudShell opened successfully.
.pem key uploaded.
SSH connection established from CloudShell.
EC2 terminal accessed successfully.
Result

Successfully connected to Linux EC2 instance using AWS CloudShell and SSH.
